speechtext:
What I say in respect to that is this: the Business Profits War Tax Act imposes a tax of a certain definite proportion of the profits in excess of 7 per cent. The consideration of this measure has no necessary connection with the earnings of any group of companies, because the taxation is imposed having regard to their profits. There is, therefore, in my view, no reason why we should not proceed with the consideration of this measure as we are doing, subject to this, that if my hon. friend desires any information as to the profits of any particular business or industry I would suggest that he place a question upon the Order Paper, and the matter can then be considered by the
104}
Government. That is the position I shall take.
